{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 disproof of Written on the Wall II Conjecture 72 of Graffiti.pc, which asserts tree(G) ≥ ⌈ecc_avg(G) + max_v λ(v)/3⌉ for every finite simple connected graph G, where tree(G) is the order of a largest induced tree, ecc_avg(G) the average eccentricity and λ(v) the independence number of the neighbourhood of v. The counterexample has 19 vertices: two 4-cycles through a common vertex, one of whose far vertices is replaced by a clique of 13 twins. Its eccentricities sum to 70, max_v λ(v) = 4 and tree(G) = 5, so the bound would be ⌈70/19 + 4/3⌉ = 6. The statement is the negation of the Formal Conjectures statement.",
